# The boundary of `checked_text`, as this crate ships it to a Nikaia program
# ([ADR-290](../../../docs/specification/adr/adr-290.md) D22, Part III 15.2).
#
# Drafted by `nikaia describe checked_text` and reviewed against `src/lib.rs`.
# The scope is #788's: the safe free functions that take no type parameter.
# An `unsafe fn` is left out, so a call to one stays NK1171. Methods and
# generic results are left out until #789. `nikaia.derived` beside this
# file records the sources it was reviewed against: a change to them
# makes `nikaia describe` refuse this file until it is reviewed again.
#
# crate: checked_text 0.1.0
version = 4

# Only with the crate's feature `map` (`cfg(feature = "map")`). A
# `std::fs::File` is lent and a `memmap2::Mmap` handed back; neither has a
# Nikaia type, so the signature claims nothing about them. The mapping does
# not keep the file. One `mmap` call, which does not pause; it fails with an
# `io::Error`; what it touches and whether it locks are left fail-closed.
[fn."checked_text::map"]
pub = true
sync = true
throws = ["?"]
signature = "(file: ?) -> ?"
